      },
      {
        "text": "Conflict arising from differing policy orientations or political affiliations can be beneficial.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The easier path in politics is compliance rather than principle.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker does not mind others attributing incorrect motives to their actions.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Principled individuals in politics often face punishment.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Conflict is productive when one is aware of it and engaged with it intentionally.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Being principled makes tasks like committee work, campaigning, leadership roles, and passing legislation more difficult.",
